inline_comments.comment:
Using `/["'[\]]/g` strips ALL quote characters globally, which corrupts titles that legitimately contain apostrophes or embedded quotes. For example, `["It's ready"]` (a double-quoted string containing an apostrophe) would be parsed correctly by the grammar but the converter would yield `Its ready` — the apostrophe is silently dropped. Similarly, `['He said "hi"']` yields `He said hi`. The converter should strip only the outer brackets and the outer quote pair, not every quote character in the string. A correct implementation:
```ts
const inner = input.slice(1, -1); // strip [ and ]
const q = inner[0];
if (q === '"' || q === "'") {
  return inner.slice(1, -1).replace(/\\(.)/g, '$1').trim();
}
return inner.trim();
```
